{\fs36\b Google Ads API Integration \line Design Documentation\b0}\par
\par
{\b Tool name:} Internal Advertising Cost Reporting Module\par
{\b Part of:} Internal Order \&amp; Revenue Management System (company-internal use)\par
{\b Access type requested:} Basic access \endash  read-only reporting\par
{\b Document version:} 1.0\par
\par
\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \par

{\fs28\b 1. Overview\b0}\par
\par
This tool is an internal, server-side module of our company\rquote s in-house order and revenue
management system. Its only purpose is to automatically retrieve daily advertising cost and
performance metrics from Google Ads and store them in our internal database, so our finance
and operations teams can compare advertising spend against sales revenue without manually
exporting reports from the Google Ads user interface.\par
\par
The tool is {\b read-only}. It does not create, edit, pause, or delete any campaigns, ads,
keywords, budgets, bids, or audiences. It performs reporting queries only. The tool is used
internally by our own staff and is {\b not} offered to third parties or resold.\par
\par

{\fs28\b 2. Business model\b0}\par
\par
Our company is a retail / e-commerce business in Vietnam selling consumer products directly to
customers through online channels. We use Google Ads (Search, Performance Max, Display,
Shopping, and Video campaigns) to drive traffic and generate sales. We manage multiple
advertising accounts under a single Manager (MCC) account.\par
\par

{\fs28\b 3. System architecture\b0}\par
\par
{\b Backend:} Python 3.13 / Django. Uses the official Google Ads Python client library
(google-ads, gRPC) to query the Google Ads API.\par
{\b Frontend:} React (TypeScript) single-page admin interface.\par
{\b Database:} PostgreSQL \endash  stores the list of managed accounts and daily cost metrics.\par
{\b Background jobs:} Celery scheduled tasks periodically refresh the daily spend data.\par
\par
{\b High-level data flow:}\par
\par
{\pard\li360 1. An administrator enters the MCC credentials once (Developer Token, OAuth2
Client ID, Client Secret, Refresh Token, Login Customer ID). Credentials are stored
server-side and are only accessible to administrators.\par
2. \ldblquote Sync Accounts\rdblquote : the tool lists the advertising accounts managed under the MCC.\par
3. \ldblquote Sync Daily Spend\rdblquote : the tool retrieves daily cost, impressions, and clicks for each
managed account and upserts them into PostgreSQL.\par
4. Internal users view advertising cost alongside order/revenue data in dashboards.\par
\par}

{\fs28\b 4. Authentication\b0}\par
\par
The tool authenticates to the Google Ads API using the standard OAuth2 flow with a long-lived
refresh token, combined with the MCC Developer Token.\par
\par
{\b OAuth scope used:} https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords\par
{\b Login customer ID:} the 10-digit Manager (MCC) account ID.\par
\par

{\fs28\b 5. API usage detail\b0}\par
\par
The tool uses only {\b GoogleAdsService.Search} (read-only GAQL SELECT queries). No mutate
or write operations of any kind are performed.\par
\par
{\b Query 1 \endash  list managed accounts:}\par
{\pard\li360\f1\fs20
SELECT customer_client.id, customer_client.descriptive_name,\line
\tab customer_client.currency_code, customer_client.status,\line
\tab customer_client.manager, customer_client.level\line
FROM customer_client\line
WHERE customer_client.level <= 1\par
\par}
{\b Query 2 \endash  daily cost and performance:}\par
{\pard\li360\f1\fs20
SELECT segments.date, metrics.cost_micros,\line
\tab metrics.impressions, metrics.clicks\line
FROM customer\line
WHERE segments.date BETWEEN '<start>' AND '<end>'\par
\par}
Cost is returned by Google in micros and divided by 1,000,000 to obtain the real amount.
Date inputs are strictly validated (canonical YYYY-MM-DD) before being used in queries to
prevent GAQL injection.\par
\par

{\fs28\b 6. Campaign types and capabilities\b0}\par
\par
{\b Campaign types covered (reporting):} Search, Performance Max, Display, Shopping, Video.\par
{\b Capability provided:} Reporting only (cost and performance retrieval). The tool provides
no campaign management, bid management, ad/creative management, keyword management,
budget management, conversion upload, or remarketing functionality.\par
\par

{\fs28\b 7. Data security and privacy\b0}\par
\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet  All API credentials are stored server-side and restricted to administrator users.\par
\bullet  Access to the configuration interface is role-protected (admin only).\par
\bullet  The tool retrieves only aggregated account-level cost and performance figures. It does
not collect or process end-user personal data.\par
\bullet  Data is used strictly for internal financial reporting and is never resold or shared with
third parties.\par
\bullet  All communication with the Google Ads API uses encrypted gRPC over TLS.\par
\par}

{\fs28\b 8. User interface (screens)\b0}\par
\par
{\pard\li360
\bullet  {\b Configuration screen:} administrators add/edit MCC credentials.\par
\bullet  {\b Accounts table:} displays the managed accounts synced from the MCC (name, customer
ID, currency, status, last sync time).\par
\bullet  {\b Daily spend view:} shows cost, impressions, and clicks per account per day for internal
reporting.\par
\par}
\par
\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20 \par
{\i This tool is for internal company use only. It performs read-only reporting and does not
modify any Google Ads entity.}\par
}
